OWED: an unselected subflow-variant-only tor refuses loudly.

Today the base handler emits `return undefined` — the call silently
does nothing (measured: program prints only "after"). Proc-variant
tors panic at runtime in the same shape; subflow variants should
match (panic parity) or refuse earlier. This pin asserts a frontend
refusal as the strictest reading; retarget if panic parity lands.
